OL,3,GNEWSAAI tools that take notes for GPs
OL,4,Acould miss vital information, study
OL,5,Asuggests
OL,6,
OL,7,FAI tools that are used to take medical
OL,8,Fnotes from patients could miss vital
OL,9,Finformation and lead to medical staff
OL,10,Fbeing deskilled, according to new
OL,11,Fresearch.
OL,13,FThe tools, called ambient AI scribes,
OL,14,Fare used by about 40% of GPs in the UK.
OL,15,FThe scribes listen to conversations
OL,16,Fbetween doctors and patients and
OL,17,Fconvert the speech to text, generating
OL,18,Fwritten notes and letters.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,425,420,260,160,0,100
PN,42402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F424A1788476147
OL,1,W5j 5Qwsj#%7k"k#j  w{j#57i
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q,.*,%-. * *,$%** %-& (,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAAI tools that take notes for GPs
OL,4,Acould miss vital information, study
OL,5,Asuggests
OL,6,
OL,7,FAcademics at University of Edinburgh
OL,8,Freviewed cases involving the scribes
OL,9,Fand found the tech had some positives,
OL,10,Fsuch as allowing clinicians to focus on
OL,11,Fcomplex tasks.
OL,13,FHowever, they also said patients could
OL,14,Fbe less forthcoming if they knew they
OL,15,Fwere being recorded and found instances
OL,16,Fwhere doctors did not recognise their
OL,17,Fnotes.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
